X:1
T:Valse Op. 69 No. 2
C:Frédéric Chopin
O:Waltz in B minor, Op. 69 No. 2 (posthumous)
N:The whole waltz as printed, each repeat played once: the B-minor theme, the
N:D-major section, the B-major trio, then back to the start. Transposed down a
N:major sixth to D minor (D major in the trio), so the highest note is A5. 19
N:lead-in notes at phrase ends would fall below C4 and are played an octave
N:higher. Notes from two Humdrum first-edition encodings (ifdo.ca, kern2abc) and
N:the flutetunes.com MIDI. Bar 124 follows the second edition and the MIDI, which
N:have an F the first edition lacks. In bar 125 both encodings read D sharp and the
N:MIDI has D natural, which I followed, since the line descends in B minor. Chords
N:from the left hand of the flutetunes.com arrangement, one per bar. The last bar
N:stops after two beats, where the pickup of the next pass comes in.
M:3/4
Q:1/4=132
L:1/8
K:Dm
